[00:41.51]Conversation One
[00:44.56]W: Hi, Mathew, congratulations! 
[00:47.29]I met Prof. Green this morning and he told me you made a Global 500 job.
[00:53.30]M: Thank you. I am thrilled too. 
[00:56.29]You also did good work passing the first round of the interview held by the GQ Investment Bank. 
[01:02.67]I'm sure you will also do well in the final interview.
[01:06.60]W: I hope so. 
[01:07.86]I also hope that you can share with me some of your successful experience, if you don't mind.
[01:14.06]M: Sure. No problem. 
[01:16.30]What do you want to know?
[01:18.40]W: How did you prepare for your interview? 
[01:20.95]Do they ask the same questions as they do in the first interview?
[01:25.25]M: No. The interviewers are top executives and the questions are quite different. 
[01:31.67]You really need to know the corporation. 
[01:34.60]Even if you researched before your first interview, review the information and read more on the company. 
[01:41.57]Show you care about the company by being able to tailor your answers to the company's vision and goals.
[01:48.86]W: Then, what kind of questions they may ask?
[01:52.08]M: I don't think you'll get the same kind of questions everywhere. 
[01:56.48]If you know somebody who already works for the company, talk to them to get a sense of what to expect from the final interview. 
[02:05.34]Ask for any insight into exactly what the interviewers are looking for.
[02:11.12]W: Good to know. What else?
[02:13.52]M: Consider your requirements and desires for salary and benefits. 
[02:18.15]Questions about these topics may arise in the final interview. 
[02:22.46]Preparing yourself to answer the questions helps you avoid being caught off guard and giving a salary range you later regret.
[02:31.14]W: I really haven't thought about that. 
[02:33.40]Oh, the bus is coming. 
[02:35.10]May I call you if I have more questions?
[02:37.77]M: Sure. See you!
[02:40.69]Questions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.
[02:45.88]1. Why does the woman say congratulations to the man?
[03:03.92]2. According to the man, what preparation should the woman make for her interview?
[03:25.78]3. Why does the man advise the woman to talk to somebody who already works for the company?
[03:46.91]4. According to the man, what kind of questions are likely to appear in the final interview?
[04:08.67]Conversation Two
