[15:12.18]Recording One
[15:14.42]Imagine you are watching the NBA Finals, there are 1.5 seconds left, and your favorite team is down by one point in game seven. 
[15:25.47]There is enough time for one last shot. 
[15:28.91]I'm guessing you know who you would like to take the last shot. 
[15:33.20]Every team has their own fan favorite superstar. 
[15:36.95]Whether your sport of choice is basketball or another sport, we all know how great athletes look and are aware of the mindset they embody. 
[15:47.64]If you were to list the mental characteristics, it would read something like: motivated, determined, courageous, focused, and so on.
[15:57.95]Would you like to embody some of these qualities? 
[16:01.72]I bet you would. 
[16:03.53]The truth is, there is no reason you can't. 
[16:07.29]That's exactly what the field of sport and performance psychology does. 
[16:12.20]It teaches athletes and everyday people how to harness their inner mental toughness. 
[16:18.51]Performance psychology is a key component in my work with athletes, performers, and executives. 
[16:25.79]On some level everyone is an athlete, perhaps your sport just happens to be financial trading, or making million-dollar sales, or writing a best-seller. 
[16:37.08]We all have an arena in which we strive to be a superstar. 
[16:41.61]We can all take something from sport psychology to jump start our performance.
[16:47.55]In sport, as in life, one of the biggest keys is knowing the end result you want and having a crystal clear vision of where you want to go. 
[16:58.94]It's very difficult to go after something if you don't know what it is you're going after. 
[17:05.07]The more detailed and vivid your goal, the better. 
[17:08.95]While goal-setting is nothing new, it's a very powerful tool when done consistently. 
[17:15.33]The field of sport and performance psychology has done some of the most rigorous research on goal-setting of all fields. 
[17:23.75]We've demonstrated positive results of setting goals time and time again.
[17:29.79]Knowing your goals will increase your motivation. 
[17:33.28]Once you know where you want to go, start breaking your long-term goals down into manageable daily actions that are process-focused. 
[17:43.58]Great athletes focus on what they can control. 
[17:46.95]Setting daily action-packed goals will help you stay focused on what you can do to ensure your long-term results come true.
